ild-golden.sh` failed with `execution environment requires native Python 3.14, found 3.13` (exit code 78).\n  - *Fix*: Set `OP_EXECUTION_PYTHON_BUNDLE` to `/home/jeremy/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.14.7-linux-x86_64-gnu` in `deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh`. Verified unchanged hash and exit 0.\n- **Error 2**: `op-release-launch deploy` failed during activation: `timeout: down: /etc/sv/tched-router: 1s, normally up, want up`.\n  - *Root Cause*: `deploy/runit/tched-router/run` line 87 was hardcoded to check for `opdbus.threetched.v1`, while candidate golden was migrated to `v2` (zeroclaw 0.8.4).\n  - *Fix*: Updated `deploy/runit/tched-router/run` to support `opdbus.threetched.v2` and upstream binary name `zeroclaw`.\n- **Error 3**: `tched-router` crashed on startup with `Error: Failed to read config file ... Permission denied (os error 13)`.\n  - *Root Cause*: `/var/lib/tched-router/config.toml` was owned by `root:root 0600`, but `deploy/runit/tched-router/run` was invoking `chpst -u jeremy:jeremy`.\n  - *Fix*: Re-aligned `tched-router/run` and `check` to run strictly as `root:root` with `USER=root`, matching the user's principle that there is no unprivileged username for this backend service.\n- **Error 4**: Attempted to test `threetched daemon` on port 8085 and received binary output / `HTTP/0.9`.\n  - *Root Cause*: Port 8085 is already bound to EMQX private wake WSS. Tested on port 8086 instead; `health` and `check` passed completely.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Active Release Slot**: Slot A (`release-9b52e195-0253-4616-8a98-2b2f16d9defb`).\n- **Services Currently Running**:\n  - `op-grpc-bridge` (PID 24013) on `10.0.0.2:8090`\n  - `op-web` (PID 26879) on `10.0.0.2:8080`\n  - `tched-router` (PID 21834) on `127.0.0.1:8084`\n  - `emqx` (PID 24785)\n  - `qdrant-recovered` container (listening on `127.0.0.1:6333` / `:6334`)\n- **Git State**:\n  - Modified: `deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh`, `deploy/runit/tched-router/run`, `deploy/runit/tched-router/check`.\n- **Operator Connection**: Connected from `10.0.0.9`. Do not alter router keys or drop this connection.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Test Cognitive Endpoints Live**:\n   - Query `cognitive` methods through D-Bus (`/org/opdbus/v1/plugins/cognitive` on `/run/opdbus/session-bus.sock`) or via gRPC `PluginService/CallMethod`:\n     - Test `cognitive.get_health`\n     - Test `cognitive.list_tools`\n     - Test `cognitive.memory_list_namespaces`\n     - Test `cognitive.memory_query` / `memory_recall` against Qdrant (`127.0.0.1:6334`) and Cozo\n   - Verify bi-temporal memory recall via `crates/op-cognitive/src/memory_store.rs` and `qdrant_shuttle.rs`.\n2. **Complete Slot B Activation**:\n   - Run `sudo ./activate-golden.sh` (or `sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch deploy` followed by `activate b`).\n   - Confirm `tched-router` stays up and clean overlay swap to Slot B succeeds.\n3. **Svelte UI (`3tched.com`) Updates**:\n   - Add \"New chat\" / \"Clear chat\" button in `src/svelte/Chat.svelte`.\n   - Hide `Personal` menu section when authenticated as the root Control Plane Chatbot.\n4. **Enforce 2-of-N Cryptographic Superadmin Policy**:\n   - Register superadmin public keys in capability policy.\n   - Enforce dual-signature gate for root delegated operations.\n5. **Run Full End-to-End Live Demo**:\n   - Ingest memory $\\rightarrow$ query via chatbot $\\rightarrow$ bi-temporal recall $\\rightarrow$ root delegation $\\rightarrow$ dynamic UI promotion.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Preserve User Connection**: Never disconnect or drop `10.0.0.9` while the operator is connected through it.\n- **Root Chatbot Invariant**: The chatbot is the single root entity on the system (`root:root`), but has zero direct execution and no internet access. All actions are delegated to bounded workers.\n- **Frontend Stack**: Strictly Svelte/SvelteKit + Vite + `@json-render/svelte`. Never introduce React or other renderers.\n- **Init Policy**: Runit